 challenged to test the  balance in their lives using a workbook  that rated them on movement nutrition  and purpose among other things  my 2020 vision is to get rid of those  fears that I now at Weight Watchers  it was Oprah's intention to partner with  WW the company formerly known as Weight  Watchers  it was started on Long Island by Jean  Medich who wanted to lose some weight  and did it with a community of women who  she would invite over to her house they  would weigh themselves that was 57 years  ago I loved the new my WW program  Oprah is now the largest shareholder in  WW but long before she had an ownership  stake  she says the point system that the  company uses helped her realize that  living well isn't about staying home and  starving yourself so when each tour stop  Oprah highlights local restaurants that  offer WW meals the Colgate's  owns low greenhouse grill in Miami there  WW menu item is shrimp and collard  greens they thought we were just  stopping by for a taste no once Nicole  caught her breath she served us some of  Chef Kareem's tasty shrimp and collard  greens which yours truly had never had  before very good as we say in Louisiana  sauce a ball  very good it was sauce a bomb good  sometimes women of color who are in a  certain financial situation don't feel  like they have access to these yes yes  so in order for you all to in court  bring us in when they can walk across  the street and actually sit down dine  with dignity with their families and be  a part of a national program like Weight  Watchers makes the world just a little  bit smaller part of wws push is wellness  that involves working on your mental  health  one of the biggest champions of mental  health education is lady gaga  we stopped by to speak with us before  taking the stage  I know kindness is your mantra Chinese  heals all things it is the most powerful  weapon that we have interpersonal Gaga  got very personal with Oprah  I will put my shame in a box all the way  over there and make it very small hmm  and say to myself I have mental health  issues I take a lot of medication to  stay on board and I'm a survivor  and I'm living and I'm thriving and I'm  strong and I'm gonna take all my life  experiences and I'm gonna share them  with the world and make it a better  place  Wow so many in the crowd were recording  with their cell phones as Lady Gaga  candidly revealed how she deals with  pain daily and she says it's caused by  fibromyalgia  a medicine called carbonic called The  Lancet me and I took a few other things  that are stress based but I want to be  very careful about say any of this you  know in a public way to tell anyone what  to take you know this is not it's not  the same for everyone and that is the  kind of real talk which Oprah is known  for getting from celebrities who remind  us that we are connected through our  struggles and with that the first stop  on Oprah's nine city tour was over  thoughts on the whole day my thought of  the whole day is wow this is  unbelievable I think this is this is so  incredible it makes me really want to  cry makes me want to cry that people  care so much that they would come out  and they would give up their Saturdays  and do this what is your intention for  every person who comes I hope people  leave with the rising and them because  you know I know that you can't come to a  motivational speech or day and instantly  change your life  but I want people to feel the rising  inside them that yearns for the more and  then have clarity about what that more  is oh they felt that let me tell you so  the interview with Lady Gaga will air on  Oprah's Facebook channel and the WWE now  Facebook channel this coming Wednesday I  was there and I'm like god I want to go  to that and it's going to Minneapolis  next week she's and she's doing nine  cities but Oprah was emotional Gaga was  emotional and you see the two of them  together  Gaga talked very candidly about being  raped about being bullied you can see  that on Oprah's Instagram it's worth  going to see the two of them together  just sort of rehashing what happened on  that day tawny she was so piercingly  personal yeah it wasn't expecting to get  that from Lady gaga she almost came  somewhat humbled you know it wasn't the  big shock in all performer that you used  it  made her so relatable yeah a so so human  she was very fragile didn't you think  that was very fragile on the stage and I  think Oprah does that in terms of  bringing people out and that's really  what she wants as we all go into 2020 to  figure it out what what propels us what  makes us happy and how do we achieve  that and it's so much more than weight  wellness on this particular tour is a  very big part of the state of mind yes  it's not your grandmother and  granddaughters Weight Watchers anymore  this is a whole new ballgame  David thanks nice job David very nice  job  you

